# 3. Project Design Phase
**Project Name:** ComicVerse AI

## High-Level System Architecture

* **Frontend Layer:**
  * `index.html`: Interactive input form where users specify prompt, main character name, setting, tone, and art style[span_0](start_span)[span_0](end_span).
  * `comic_preview.html`: Live preview interface showing panel images with corresponding story dialogues[span_1](start_span)[span_1](end_span).
  * `export_success.html`: Confirmation screen with direct download link for the generated PDF[span_2](start_span)[span_2](end_span).

* **Backend Framework (FastAPI):**
  * `main.py`: Entry point for server routing and template rendering[span_3](start_span)[span_3](end_span).
  * `routes.py`: Manages pipeline orchestration and user input processing[span_4](start_span)[span_4](end_span).

* **AI Generation Services:**
  * `Gemini Flash API`: Generates the initial panel-by-panel story outline[span_5](start_span)[span_5](end_span).
  * `Gemini Pro API`: Produces full narrative text and character dialogues for each panel[span_6](start_span)[span_6](end_span).
  * `Hugging Face Diffusers (Stable Diffusion)`: Renders tailored comic artwork based on scene descriptions and selected art style[span_7](start_span)[span_7](end_span).

* **Layout & Export Module:**
  * `layout_builder.py`: Combines generated images, panel titles, and story text into unified panel objects[span_8](start_span)[span_8](end_span).
  * `exporters.py`: Compiles the layout into a multi-page PDF using FPDF and saves a timestamped output file[span_9](start_span)[span_9](end_span).

## Data Execution Flow

1. User submits comic preferences via input form[span_10](start_span)[span_10](end_span).
2. Backend receives request and calls Gemini Flash to generate story outline[span_11](start_span)[span_11](end_span).
3. Gemini Pro expands outline into full dialogue and narrative script[span_12](start_span)[span_12](end_span).
4. Stable Diffusion generates matching panel images for each scene[span_13](start_span)[span_13](end_span).
5. `layout_builder.py` constructs structured panel layouts[span_14](start_span)[span_14](end_span).
6. `exporters.py` compiles final output into PDF format for preview and download[span_15](start_span)[span_15](end_span).

